          "content": "\n\nYes, that'll be a problem. The script uses boto3 (for DynamoDB polling, CloudFormation lookup, Cognito auth) and those calls will fail once your credentials expire. The `requests` call to AgentCore also uses a Cognito token (not AWS creds), so that part is fine — but the polling and reset steps need valid AWS credentials.\n\nOptions:\n\n1. **Refresh before bed, hope it finishes** — 6 tiers × ~1-1.5hr each = ~6-9 hours. If creds last 24hr you're probably fine.\n\n2. **Have the script read `~/.aws/credentials` fresh on each iteration** — boto3 already does this by default (it doesn't cache credentials across client instantiations). Since the script creates new boto3 clients/resources inside each function call, refreshing `~/.aws/credentials` mid-run will be picked up on the next poll cycle. You just need to paste new creds before the old ones expire.\n\n3. **Add a credential check at the start of each tier** — pause and warn if creds are about to expire.\n\nOption 2 is actually already how it works — boto3 reads `~/.aws/credentials` on each new client creation. The issue is the script reuses `boto3.resource(\"dynamodb\")` inside `wait_for_completion` which creates the client once and polls for up to 6 hours with it.\n\nLet me fix the polling to create a fresh client periodically:",
