          "content": "\n\nYes — `AUTOTUNE_SESSION_ID` is set as an env var before the agent starts, so any tool can access it via `os.environ[\"AUTOTUNE_SESSION_ID\"]`. The `upload_config` tool could easily append a session prefix/suffix.\n\nBut do you actually need this? The reset script clears all custom configs between runs, so there shouldn't be name collisions across experiment tiers. The only scenario where it'd matter is if you skip the reset or run multiple experiments concurrently against the same IDP stack.\n\nIf you do want it, the simplest approach would be to have `upload_config` auto-append the first 8 chars of the session ID to the version name and tell the agent in the tool response what the final name is. Want me to add that?"
